  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The yearly changes in the population census of a town for four consecutive years are, respectively, \\(25\\%\\) increase, \\(25\\%\\) increase, \\(25\\%\\) decrease, \\(25\\%\\) decrease. The net change over the four years, to the nearest percent, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "-12"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The final population is multiplied by \\[ (1.25)^2(0.75)^2=\\frac{225}{256}\\approx0.879. \\] This is a decrease of about \\(12.1\\%,\\) which rounds to \\(12\\%.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Represent each increase by a factor of \\(1.25\\) and each decrease by \\(0.75\\)",
        "Compare \\(1.25^2\\cdot0.75^2\\) with \\(1\\)"
      ],
